{"id": "clm:02e3c67fd9f2adf69657d32fd8c134bf90eeb7763a26c20eea8a1b87df7c3d32", "type": "statement", "text": "$toObject retains the last value for duplicate field names. RFC 8259 recommends unique names because receivers differ; ECMA-404 defines syntax without mandating how a programming language internalizes JSON. Last-value behavior is a MongoDB mapping rule, not a universal JSON guarantee. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8259", "https://ecma-international.org/publications-and-standards/standards/ecma-404/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:520537e470ae5d0c6f4aaf92d6c48050700498edc5cd5aec910ea73a64a9de59", "ev:5e2779d5518c7760c32317fd7edcf29a9b6f6087926812b3252b74ccfc14a5f2", "ev:b27369f3747d351e5385509e45bc9762a6018741832f812e39b300dbc200109a"]}
{"id": "clm:2a0fb51ea8eec8449aadc0cea53e273be6ae398fce0adadec1303f186c7ea329", "type": "statement", "text": "Implementation-derived boundary in MongoDB r8.3.0: existing BSON arrays and objects do not get identity conversions to array/object, nor native array-to-object or object-to-array conversions. The dispatch tables lack these entries and raise ConversionFailure; onError can handle that failure. This was checked in source, not by executing a server. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.3.0/src/mongo/db/exec/expression/evaluate_math.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ee2ffe135bb85de479670efd236d7e18b7ca966f61cd5da8c8721cb479160f1", "ev:585df6beea8a67faa31b377f2db3e4eb14b7107ab75c5d7255d6fc84ed11e4a2", "ev:b3814ab2ebcf50e1eea4942f8dae202b0e2880408c2a9fe3dd8507765c749384"]}
{"id": "clm:d76a0625a38c75ce95aa0f8363a9233af77bbcf3141152a56cff7f3cef7de88e", "type": "statement", "text": "A valid JSON scalar is not sufficient input for these container parsers: both document errors for \"123\". RFC 8259 permits top-level scalar JSON values, so this failure is an operator acceptance boundary rather than proof that scalar JSON is invalid. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md", "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8259"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:41e50e1cfaed7bf00eafac93e923e995d826f7e7198b30c8c2cff117b12b738d", "ev:a34b48ab05d21248ebfe3301ad7918e8f15d6f1b17bb79bb0f32ea01262e963e", "ev:b8745f069a47c8e0525cdb590aed5db6d68153560f20d2cec9c4d3749073fdb3"]}
{"id": "clm:c04060fd5182cef8e3e1b7a79a2560bc8c91eb8262143d6d695c99ea223ec789", "type": "statement", "text": "The documented non-null inputs are a JSON-object string for $toObject, and a JSON-array string or supported subtype-9 binData vector for $toArray. Numeric input such as 123 is an unsupported conversion to array, rather than automatic singleton wrapping. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:044a28048df451d93492efae4d108a3eb851f059a2cf6c6a4c9fb34e58142bce", "ev:a34b48ab05d21248ebfe3301ad7918e8f15d6f1b17bb79bb0f32ea01262e963e", "ev:bf0e89b311c2b113109665678f1c4f57879ae4f3e12e8adb7e5632bdfb170c5a"]}
{"id": "clm:28dc8adbe2de6892bd08d41731a76866f9571b3a2af63048221887663a59e0a0", "type": "statement", "text": "These shorthands parse ordinary JSON containers: Extended JSON wrappers such as $oid and $date remain nested data rather than producing their BSON special types. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:24e547b389c2743851757912c7abf2b163eea917029e81205e031d42cbda92e4", "ev:fef1d69bf6ee60a91e878c77d87595b7c5395461a65b6fb32a9e10e7ed43bd4c"]}
{"id": "clm:8728a0fcc215f06fb9c3c89285f6587c7922e41db373ba3bff6fa65929781d96", "type": "statement", "text": "ECMA-404 defines JSON syntax without prescribing how a programming language internalizes it. BSON type mapping and conversion acceptance must therefore come from MongoDB's contract, rather than being inferred solely from JSON syntax. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://ecma-international.org/publications-and-standards/standards/ecma-404/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:66f019971682ce146f3779cfa5b260f115250a4b0643bf1470d39be8f605f97a", "ev:b27369f3747d351e5385509e45bc9762a6018741832f812e39b300dbc200109a"]}
{"id": "clm:e7c4fb12496f7cd43ac2a55439f746a6f578afd5408e7824e7c23a6637ade525", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB 8.3 introduces conversion of JSON array and object strings through $convert and the $toArray/$toObject shorthand expressions. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.3/release-notes/8.3/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6c05701711bef805358a5cb7b2d5609f87cf36f382eb30d1acd7909d480de348"]}
{"id": "clm:7df598877059a7a4b63634cfae43d13840708d3d872746b61d9edf82f2eb2197", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB 8.3 introduced string-to-container conversions: {$toArray: expression} abbreviates {$convert: {input: expression, to: 'array'}}, and $toObject abbreviates the corresponding to: 'object' conversion. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.3/release-notes/8.3/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:308a84c9c9f38163f9916592badce97dd724abbc0fca5002e102d093c0351dc4", "ev:6c05701711bef805358a5cb7b2d5609f87cf36f382eb30d1acd7909d480de348", "ev:f75b40c8e21507bdad5498bdbf5b204c17073cd19353ef94e706932a20914cc9"]}
{"id": "clm:7c9131dfc5a724493bf4654481cf74c6b71b108bea5d87ef1c9096451823e974", "type": "statement", "text": "String parsing requires strict JSON: comments and trailing commas are rejected. $toArray requires a top-level array and rejects \"{}\"; $toObject requires a top-level object and rejects \"[]\". (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:41e50e1cfaed7bf00eafac93e923e995d826f7e7198b30c8c2cff117b12b738d", "ev:7f1d055dfb7240b472747619659b6c1cbeaea7fb9690e2090718d487060234c6", "ev:d05e494d74d258e72e4177a45d21d1b558952c6c5b008054c088dd33a43d7203", "ev:db7f3d9acb74bf0d031d95ee4d248873c3f0823e373fdc030b57d5fd6bc8beb5"]}
{"id": "clm:8bb90cf4181a3911ed5e9ce6a62bc67dad8701cd2a5d6115c89e3acef721a2ba", "type": "statement", "text": "Both shorthands return null for null or missing input. Conversion failures stop the aggregation; use $convert with onError and onNull to supply explicit fallback values. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:02ab2abaa8561d13cca10cc6df98321511e401ed01642c96feebcb4f5999afaf", "ev:58ff48a8116ce12e61b28fca106b229b9915f69520b1b50716c71d5a6cce1c5a", "ev:5a569af313506c900524084ccce62b410cd075c443973a98663081091668cddf", "ev:bfb07f7c4a30381a8c0830fbefe5143d51de9e24bf1f69f3bf234ead5df6a8d6"]}
{"id": "clm:d449936b17b3c0d7992fb30152429f65453bc2c0409a8b1d3aa99f4d648fd358", "type": "statement", "text": "The documented input table for $toObject lists strings and null/missing. $toArray additionally supports subtype-9 vector binData: PACKED_BIT becomes booleans, INT8 integers, and FLOAT32 doubles. A native integer such as 123 is an unsupported array conversion. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:044a28048df451d93492efae4d108a3eb851f059a2cf6c6a4c9fb34e58142bce", "ev:a34b48ab05d21248ebfe3301ad7918e8f15d6f1b17bb79bb0f32ea01262e963e", "ev:e6685c249a2343337ac522c9cdad50558005111b3dd93a878cdcbf31b9a91e6d"]}
{"id": "clm:538e65addeda254398b7379fb64bedb03fd2341d00598cb1a83aa315f6cd717f", "type": "statement", "text": "JSON syntax permits escaped U+0000 in strings, but MongoDB's object conversion rejects an embedded null byte in a field name. The documented input containing a key nam\\u0000e fails with 'Illegal embedded null byte'. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md", "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8259"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:33fcc8fc2aac94972f431c5d35b0f4ae98fcf192dc6f2da6b2094b722db3571d", "ev:ab38118185c7a536bcb1f0d00a020b7f451e28f3afc37139ff2493deb3fe4ff4"]}
{"id": "clm:1061a4f5b60d7bbf386e9d6e495e334f7195a11c70ebd9078855303b28efe924", "type": "statement", "text": "String inputs require valid JSON without comments or trailing commas, and their top-level container must match the target. Thus '{}' fails for $toArray, '[]' fails for $toObject, and the standalone string '123' fails for both. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/convert.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:41e50e1cfaed7bf00eafac93e923e995d826f7e7198b30c8c2cff117b12b738d", "ev:7f1d055dfb7240b472747619659b6c1cbeaea7fb9690e2090718d487060234c6", "ev:a34b48ab05d21248ebfe3301ad7918e8f15d6f1b17bb79bb0f32ea01262e963e", "ev:db7f3d9acb74bf0d031d95ee4d248873c3f0823e373fdc030b57d5fd6bc8beb5"]}
{"id": "clm:e768b55bf7289c0adaca04f3f6d32fbc5f8a880b49e718c236fde69278bc8b75", "type": "statement", "text": "Parsed integers map to BSON int within signed 32-bit range, long within signed 64-bit range, and double beyond that range; decimal-point or exponent notation maps to double. Large integers can therefore lose precision. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toArray.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Native JSON container shorthand parsing and type boundaries"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toObject.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:8038e654f670754c7b5e770a9089363223f7bf2c42573707b155823bd5cf9fb0", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b7c45349c0144ed349ccefeabc45240ed2cd62f59ed334472804b5deacd89456", "ev:dd8d540e54d077f6919a7af7d4bfac9d5731a15d78575f02d8f2f5f7e24863cd"]}
